{
  "$comment": "Named page-filter presets. A page's `filters` array may hold a STRING naming one of these instead of repeating the object; `normalizeMeta` in app/lib/pages.js expands it (an array preset, like a date range, splices in; an object preset becomes one filter). This is DATA, not behaviour: the field shapes are what fourteen page manifests were spelling out identically. A page still writes its own filters inline where they are unique (the payment `type` select, the `applyDate` check). An unknown preset name is dropped AND logged, so a typo is not a silently missing filter.",
